   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Shower** (1 review): Review calls this track a priceless gem from the golden years [2]\n- **Doctor Wu (Steely Dan cover)** (1 review): The performance is described as an absolutely killer version of the Steely Dan cover [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Take A Letter Maria (R. B. Greaves cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Itzcuintli-Totzli Days**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Shower**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Tulsa Imperative**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Chanson Du Bon Chose**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Edvard Munch**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Standard Bitter Love Song #2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Cutter**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: (string break), Black Molly, (video for New Britain), Twin Human Highway Flares, Baboon [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg1997-06-12.aud.128mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 23 songs; 59 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Whacky banter and peripheral dialogue pull the listener into the basement atmosphere [2]",
